{"step_index":98,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T13:59:02Z","input_tokens":2863,"cache_read_tokens":95506,"output_tokens":1058,"thinking":"The server logs confirm the app.js and data modules are accessible and returning 200 OK responses, indicating no immediate issues with module loading or server reachability. The function `generate_tax_suggestions` is verified as implemented in JavaScript within the utils folder, and is confirmed to use Gemini 2.5 Flash as requested.\n\n\nThe analysis reveals two versions of the tax suggestion logic, one for frontend execution and another in Python. The prompt outlines the desired output format: ITR form recommendation with justification, GST ITC opportunity/risk assessment including warning about unverified supplier GSTINs, and a reminder about the advance tax deadline. UI design specifications include a \"Tax & ITR Insights\" tab with pills for the recommended form, deemed net profit, and estimated tax liability.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/README.md","Replacement":"### 5. Tax & ITR Insights (Gemini 2.5 Flash + Sec 44AD Engine)\n- **Deterministic Presumptive Tax Calculation:**\n  - Deemed Profit calculated strictly in code under **Section 44AD** at **6% digital / 8% cash**.\n  - Estimated Tax Liability computed under the **New Tax Regime (Section 115BAC)** with Section 87A rebate checks.\n- **3 Dynamic KPI Pills:**\n  - **Pill 1:** `Recommended Form: ITR-4 (Presumptive Scheme - Sec 44AD)`\n  - **Pill 2:** `Deemed Net Profit: ₹X,XX,XXX (Calculated at 6% digital / 8% cash)`\n  - **Pill 3:** `Estimated Tax Liability: ₹X,XXX (Computed via New Regime)`\n- **Advisory Callout Box:** Plain-English summary explaining how keeping supplier GSTINs verified maximizes Input Tax Credit (ITC) and lowers tax outgo.\n- **`generate_tax_suggestions(audit_summary, calculated_tax)`:**\n  - Uses **Gemini 2.5 Flash** to provide 3 concise bullet points (Recommended ITR Form, GST ITC Opportunity/Risk, Advance Tax deadline of March 15) with the mandatory disclaimer: *\"Not tax advice; verify with your CA.\"*\n\n### 6. Client-Side Privacy & Masking","Target":"### 5. Client-Side Privacy & Masking"}}]}
