{"step_index":100,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T13:59:13Z","input_tokens":3223,"cache_read_tokens":96321,"output_tokens":1119,"content":"### Implementation Complete\n\nWe have created the function `generate_tax_suggestions(audit_summary, calculated_tax)` powered by **Gemini 2.5 Flash** and integrated the **Tax & ITR Insights** card right below the invoice audit report.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The `generate_tax_suggestions` Function\n\nThe function is available in both **JavaScript** for the frontend ([`utils/taxSuggestions.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/taxSuggestions.js)) and **Python** ([`utils/tax_suggestions.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/tax_suggestions.py)).\n\n#### Python Implementation ([`utils/tax_suggestions.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/tax_suggestions.py))\n```python\ndef generate_tax_suggestions(audit_summary: dict, calculated_tax: dict, api_key: str = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generate tax preparation suggestions for small Indian retail shopkeepers using Gemini 2.5 Flash.\n    Input Context:\n      - Total turnover and deemed profit (calculated by code)\n      - Number of invoices analyzed\n      - Total GST paid on purchases (potential ITC)\n      - Invoices missing GSTIN (disallowed ITC)\n    \"\"\"\n    ...\n```\n\n#### Exact Prompt Used:\n```text\nYou are a tax preparation assistant for small Indian retail shopkeepers.\nGiven this pre-calculated financial data:\n{data}\n\nProvide 3 concise bullet points:\n1. Recommended ITR Form: (e.g., ITR-4 Sugam under Sec 44AD vs ITR-3) with a 1-sentence reason.\n2. GST ITC Opportunity / Risk: Explain how much Input Tax Credit can be claimed from audited bills and warn about unverified supplier GSTINs.\n3. Advance Tax & Action Item: Remind them of the March 15 advance tax deadline.\n\nTone: Grounded, simple English, no complex jargon. Include a clear disclaimer: 'Not tax advice; verify with your CA.'\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. UI Dashboard Addition: \"Tax & ITR Insights\"\n\nIn [`AuditScorecard.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/AuditScorecard.js), right below the itemized invoice audit table and compliance checks, we added the **Tax & ITR Insights** card:\n\n1. **Pill 1:** `Recommended Form: ITR-4 (Presumptive Scheme - Sec 44AD)`\n2. **Pill 2:** `Deemed Net Profit: ₹2,44,800.00 (Calculated at 6% digital / 8% cash)`\n3. **Pill 3:** `Estimated Tax Liability: ₹0.00 (Computed via New Regime - Sec 115BAC / 87A)`\n4. **Advisory Callout Box:**\n   > *\"Every rupee of GST shown on your purchase invoices can directly offset your GST tax liability via **Input Tax Credit (ITC)**. However, Indian tax laws (Section 16 of the CGST Act) mandate that ITC is strictly disallowed if your supplier does not have an active, verified GSTIN. Always verify supplier GSTINs on AUDIT IT before making payments to protect your ITC and avoid paying tax twice!\"*\n5. **Gemini 2.5 Flash 3-Bullet Summary & Action Item:**\n   - **Bullet 1 (ITR Form):** Recommends ITR-4 Sugam under Section 44AD presumptive scheme without maintaining bulky account books.\n   - **Bullet 2 (GST ITC Opportunity/Risk):** Dynamically informs how much ITC is eligible vs disallowed based on whether the supplier's GSTIN is valid (e.g. alerts when GSTIN is missing on Sample 3).\n   - **Bullet 3 (Advance Tax):** Reminds the shopkeeper to pay 100% of their advance tax by the **March 15 deadline** to prevent penal interest under Section 234B/234C.\n   - **Disclaimer:** *\"⚖️ Not tax advice; verify with your CA.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Verification\n\nYou can test this in the running app at [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000):\n1. Select **Sample 1: Clean Bill** or **Sample 3: Missing GSTIN**.\n2. Scroll to the **Tax & ITR Insights** card below the line items table.\n3. Observe how Pill 1, Pill 2, Pill 3, and the advisory callout update dynamically based on the audited bill's GST status.\n4. Click **\"✨ Gemini 2.5 Flash\"** to re-trigger the AI recommendations on demand."}
{"step_index":101,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T14:02:02Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\ngreat now make the app functioning with real time bills and calculations based on inputs with the suitable outputs\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-11-02T19:32:02+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":102,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T14:02:02Z","input_tokens":3254,"cache_read_tokens":97494,"output_tokens":3835,"thinking":"The objective is to enable real-time bill creation and calculation within the web application, incorporating both manual input and image-based uploads. This involves implementing an interactive bill editor and real-time upload functionality for existing bills.\n\n\nDeveloping real-time bill creation requires an interactive editor capable of handling manual input and image uploads, with fields for vendor details, GSTIN, invoice information, and line items. Real-time recalculations must occur with every input change, affecting item amounts, subtotals, and tax calculations, including CGST, SGST, IGST, discrepancies, and estimated profit/tax. The system needs to provide live updating visual invoice previews, discrepancy notes, and downloadable audit slips.\n\n\nInvoice rendering currently works, but direct bill editing capabilities are absent. The application needs features for direct input modifications like adding/removing line items, adjusting tax rates, and editing vendor details directly on the bill preview. A critical enhancement would be the ability to toggle between the rendered HTML bill and the original uploaded image, with interactive canvas overlays for image-based edits.\n\n\nReal-time bill functionality necessitates OCR integration for image uploads and a manual entry interface. Tesseract.js appears suitable for client-side OCR, allowing immediate text extraction from uploaded images. This will facilitate automatic bill parsing and field population, enhancing usability. The Gemini API can be integrated to refine image-to-JSON extractions when an API key is provided, improving accuracy.\n\n\nAdding a tax rate selector alongside manual CGST/SGST/IGST input enables flexible tax calculations. GSTIN input validation against the 15-character format, with visual feedback, will ensure data integrity. A \"Declared Grand Total\" input will allow for instant discrepancy checks against calculated totals.\n\n\nEnhanced file handling will store the uploaded image URL or Base64 data for toggling between the digitized invoice and original image in the `InvoiceViewer`. Client-side OCR parsing with Tesseract.js, using regex for extraction, will also be added.\n\nThe `InvoiceViewer` will support rendering the digitized invoice synced with inputs and the uploaded image with interactive bounding boxes and a toggle. The audit scorecard will switch from `change` to `input` events for instant recalculations, including add/remove item buttons, editable GSTIN/total inputs, tax rate presets, and state tax toggles. An auto-fix discrepancy button and a turnover/ratio slider are planned for tax insights.\n\n\nThe \"Share on WhatsApp\" and \"Manually Audit a Bill\" buttons will be integrated, and `annualTurnover` and `digitalPercent` in the tax calculator will be made configurable through UI inputs. The system will manage input focus in real-time, handling image URLs for custom uploads and facilitating blank bill creation. Input focus preservation is crucial for a smooth user experience; DOM re-renders should selectively update only the calculated fields, or the active element and cursor position should be restored post-render to avoid blurring and ensure smooth typing. The tax calculator component will be inspected to confirm the input enhancements.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"// Deterministic Tax & ITR Calculator for Small Indian Retail Shopkeepers\n// Core Rule: \"Code does the math, deterministic calculations only\"\nimport { round2 } from \"./auditEngine.js\";\n\n/**\n * Calculates turnover, deemed profit under Sec 44AD, and estimated tax under New Regime\n * @param {Object} invoice\n * @param {Object} audit\n * @param {Object} [settings] - Optional user overrides for turnover and digital ratio\n */\nexport function calculateTaxMetrics(invoice, audit, settings = {}) {\n  const totalGstOnBill = round2((Number(invoice.cgst) || 0) + (Number(invoice.sgst) || 0) + (Number(invoice.igst) || 0));\n  const isGstinValid = audit.gstinValid;\n\n  const eligibleItc = isGstinValid ? totalGstOnBill : 0;\n  const blockedItc = isGstinValid ? 0 : totalGstOnBill;\n  const missingGstinCount = isGstinValid ? 0 : 1;\n\n  // Annualized turnover: default to ₹36,00,000 or user slider value\n  const annualTurnover = Number(settings.annualTurnover) || 3600000;\n  \n  // Digital vs Cash ratio: default 60% digital, 40% cash\n  const digitalRatio = settings.digitalRatio !== undefined ? Number(settings.digitalRatio) : 0.60;\n  const cashRatio = round2(1 - digitalRatio);\n\n  // Section 44AD Presumptive Profit: 6% for digital turnover, 8% for cash turnover\n  const digitalProfit = (annualTurnover * digitalRatio) * 0.06;\n  const cashProfit = (annualTurnover * cashRatio) * 0.08;\n  const deemedProfit = round2(digitalProfit + cashProfit);\n\n  // Estimated Tax under New Tax Regime (Section 115BAC)\n  // Slabs:\n  // Up to ₹3,00,000: Nil\n  // ₹3,00,001 to ₹6,00,000: 5%\n  // ₹6,00,001 to ₹9,00,000: 10%\n  // ₹9,00,001 to ₹12,00,000: 15%\n  // ₹12,00,001 to ₹15,00,000: 20%\n  // Above ₹15,00,000: 30%\n  // Rebate under Section 87A: If total income <= ₹7,00,000, tax liability is ₹0.\n  let baseTax = 0;\n  if (deemedProfit > 700000) {\n    if (deemedProfit <= 600000) {\n      baseTax = (deemedProfit - 300000) * 0.05;\n    } else if (deemedProfit <= 900000) {\n      baseTax = 15000 + (deemedProfit - 600000) * 0.10;\n    } else if (deemedProfit <= 1200000) {\n      baseTax = 45000 + (deemedProfit - 900000) * 0.15;\n    } else if (deemedProfit <= 1500000) {\n      baseTax = 90000 + (deemedProfit - 1200000) * 0.20;\n    } else {\n      baseTax = 150000 + (deemedProfit - 1500000) * 0.30;\n    }\n  }\n\n  // 4% Health & Education Cess\n  const estimatedTaxLiability = round2(baseTax * 1.04);\n\n  const audit_summary = {\n    total_turnover: annualTurnover,\n    deemed_profit: deemedProfit,\n    number_of_invoices_analyzed: 1,\n    current_invoice_total: audit.calculated_total,\n    total_gst_paid_on_purchases: totalGstOnBill,\n    eligible_itc: eligibleItc,\n    invoices_missing_gstin: missingGstinCount,\n    disallowed_itc: blockedItc,\n    vendor_name: invoice.vendor_name || \"Supplier\",\n    supplier_gstin: invoice.gstin || \"MISSING\",\n    digital_ratio: digitalRatio,\n    cash_ratio: cashRatio\n  };\n\n  const calculated_tax = {\n    recommended_form: \"ITR-4 (Presumptive Scheme - Sec 44AD)\",\n    annual_turnover: annualTurnover,\n    digital_percent: Math.round(digitalRatio * 100),\n    cash_percent: Math.round(cashRatio * 100),\n    deemed_net_profit: deemedProfit,\n    profit_computation_basis: `Calculated at 6% digital (${Math.round(digitalRatio * 100)}%) / 8% cash (${Math.round(cashRatio * 100)}%)`,\n    estimated_tax_liability: estimatedTaxLiability,\n    tax_regime: \"New Regime (Section 115BAC)\",\n    rebate_87a_applied: deemedProfit <= 700000,\n    eligible_itc: eligibleItc,\n    blocked_itc: blockedItc\n  };\n\n  return { audit_summary, calculated_tax };\n}\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/taxCalculator.js"}}]}
